{"id":"VHH__random__voronoise","collection":"VHH","category":"random","source_path":"VHH/random/voronoise.json","root_names":["VHH::Core::Random::voronoise"],"counts":{"nodes":30,"connections":69,"values":10,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Generates a voronoi pattern based on the surface points on an object by generating a random scattering of feature points and calculating the voronoi diagram.","documentation_search":"voronoise Generates a voronoi pattern based on the surface points on an object by generating a random scattering of feature points and calculating the voronoi diagram. Input geo in The input object, the fineness of detail in the resulting output depends on the number of points in this geo. control points input An array of positions, allowing you to input your own control points. If this array is empty, the compound will generate points for you based on the settings in the noise settings. scatter mode What kind of scatter to perform. Random gives a uniform pseudo-random distribution. This is the closest to truly random, but exhibits clumps and bare patches that may be unwanted for some purposes. BlueNoise gives a \"blue noise\" distribution. This is also referred to as a \"quasi-random\" or \"low discrepancy\" distribution. It provides a more even distribution, with points more equally spaced. BlueNoiseMaximal gives a similar distribution to BlueNoise. This gives the most evenly-spaced distribution, but is the slowest to compute. frequency How many random points to scatter on the object. seed The seed for the random number generator. normalize diagnostic The output of the voronoise is distances to the first and second scattered point, this will normalize those distances to a 0-1 range. color diagnostic A random color array applied to the voronoi cells. Output out geometry This is a pass-through node, your geometry is unchanged. out first distance The distance to the closest voronoi point (the distance within each cell). out second distance The distance to the next closest voronoi point (the distance to the next cell).","port_names":["color_diagnostic","control_points_input","frequency","geo_in","normalize_diagnostic","out_first_distance","out_geometry","out_second_distance","scatter_mode","seed"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::array_bounds","Core::Array::array_is_empty","Core::Array::first_in_array","Core::Array::get_from_array","Core::Array::sort_array_with_indices","Core::Conversion::scalar_to_vector3","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Graph::terminal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::change_range","Core::Math::length","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::subtract","Core::Randomization::random_value_array","Core::Type_Conversion::to_float","Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material","Geometry::Properties::get_point_position","Geometry::Properties::set_geo_property","Modeling::Points::scatter_points","for_each_in_control","for_each_in_points","voro_simple"],"dependencies_search":[],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Core::Random::voronoise","uri_imported":"file:///voronoise.json","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/voronoise.md"},"documentation_file":"VHH/docs/voronoise.md","documentation":"### ***voronoise***\nGenerates a voronoi pattern based on the surface points on an object by generating a random scattering of feature points and calculating the voronoi diagram.<br />\n\n***\n## Input\n<span style=\"color:#90A3F4\">***geo_in***</span>\n<br />The input object, the fineness of detail in the resulting output depends on the number of points in this geo.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***control_points_input***</span>\n<br />An array of positions, allowing you to input your own control points.  If this array is empty, the compound will generate points for you based on the settings in the `noise` settings.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***scatter_mode***</span>\n<br />What kind of scatter to perform.\n* Random gives a uniform pseudo-random distribution. This is the closest to truly random, but exhibits clumps and bare patches that may be unwanted for some purposes.\n* BlueNoise gives a \"blue noise\" distribution. This is also referred to as a \"quasi-random\" or \"low discrepancy\" distribution. It provides a more even distribution, with points more equally spaced.\n* BlueNoiseMaximal gives a similar distribution to BlueNoise. This gives the most evenly-spaced distribution, but is the slowest to compute.\n\n<span style=\"color:#62CFD9\">***frequency***</span>\n<br />How many random points to scatter on the object.\n\n<span style=\"color:#62CFD9\">***seed***</span>\n<br />The seed for the random number generator.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***normalize_diagnostic***</span>\n<br />The output of the `voronoise` is distances to the first and second scattered point, this will normalize those distances to a 0-1 range.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***color_diagnostic***</span>\n<br />A random color array applied to the voronoi cells.\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#90A3F4\">***out_geometry***</span>\n<br />This is a pass-through node, your geometry is unchanged.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***out_first_distance***</span>\n<br />The distance to the closest voronoi point (the distance within each cell).\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***out_second_distance***</span>\n<br />The distance to the next closest voronoi point (the distance to the next cell).","ports":[{"name":"geo_in","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"frequency","direction":"input","type":"long","default":"80"},{"name":"scatter_mode","direction":"input","type":"Modeling::Points::ScatteringMode","default":"BlueNoise"},{"name":"seed","direction":"input","type":"long","default":"975"},{"name":"out_geometry","direction":"output","type":"Object"},{"name":"out_first_distance","direction":"output","type":"array<float>"},{"name":"out_second_distance","direction":"output","type":"array<float>"},{"name":"normalize_diagnostic","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"true"},{"name":"color_diagnostic","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"false"},{"name":"control_points_input","direction":"input","type":"array<Math::float3>"}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"true"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"true"}],"counts":{"nodes":30,"connections":69,"values":10,"nested_compounds":4},"node_types":{"Core::Logic::if":3,"Core::Array::get_from_array":3,"Core::Array::first_in_array":3,"Core::Math::subtract":2,"Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material":2,"voro_simple":1,"Modeling::Points::scatter_points":1,"Geometry::Properties::get_point_position":1,"Core::Randomization::random_value_array":1,"Core::Graph::terminal":1,"Core::Math::multiply":1,"Core::Type_Conversion::to_float":1,"Core::Graph::pass":1,"Core::Conversion::scalar_to_vector3":1,"Core::Array::array_bounds":1,"Core::Math::change_range":1,"Core::Array::array_is_empty":1,"Geometry::Properties::set_geo_property":1,"for_each_in_points":1,"for_each_in_control":1,"Core::Array::sort_array_with_indices":1,"Core::Math::length":1},"custom_dependencies":{},"nodes":[{"path":"root","name":"voro_simple","type":"voro_simple"},{"path":"root","name":"scatter_points","type":"Modeling::Points::scatter_points"},{"path":"root","name":"get_point_position","type":"Geometry::Properties::get_point_position"},{"path":"root","name":"random_value_array","type":"Core::Randomization::random_value_array"},{"path":"root","name":"terminal1","type":"Core::Graph::terminal","fan_in_ports":{"final":[],"proxy":[],"diagnostic":["out_geometry"]},"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"true"}]},{"path":"root","name":"multiply","type":"Core::Math::multiply"},{"path":"root","name":"to_float","type":"Core::Type_Conversion::to_flo